Changes to OCCT (V8_0_1) for the Open CAD Viewer. Applied by wasm/scripts/build-occt.sh.

- STEP external references: read the document format from where the CAx-IF practice (External
  References 3.1, 6.3.2) and OCCT's own writer put it, a 'document format' REPRESENTATION with a
  'data format' item; OCCT looked in SHAPE_REPRESENTATIONs only, so for those files the format was
  never read and every reference was followed as a STEP file.
- Follow every STEP Part 21 format name of the practices ('STEP AP242', 'STEP AP203E2',
  'STEP AP214 CC06', 'ISO 10303-242', ...), not only 'STEP AP203' and 'STEP AP214', and not the
  AP242 XML one. New public STEPCAFControl_Reader::IsStepExternFormat, so applications that stage
  the files themselves use the same rule.

